        276.8971862792969,
        272.6158752441406,
        286.08819580078125
      ],
      "text": "ART: antiretroviral therapy; CI: confidence interval; NA: not applicable",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 7.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        297.38232421875,
        527.424560546875,
        311.8253479003906
      ],
      "text": "As a point-of-care biomedical test, CRP represents an opportunity for enhancing TB screening among",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        311.38232421875,
        527.4265747070312,
        325.8253479003906
      ],
      "text": "people living with HIV. Health staff and patients might be more motivated to pursue a confirmatory",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        325.3822937011719,
        527.4234619140625,
        339.8253173828125
      ],
      "text": "diagnostic test following a positive screen for CRP. The specificity and predictive value of the test for",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        339.3822937011719,
        527.4511108398438,
        353.8253173828125
      ],
      "text": "detecting TB, however, will likely be reduced in settings with a lower TB prevalence than in those",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        353.3822937011719,
        206.69412231445312,
        367.8253173828125
      ],
      "text": "included in the meta-analysis.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        381.206298828125,
        229.59170532226562,
        395.6272888183594
      ],
      "text": "Recommendation 4: Chest X-ray",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiboldItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        395.3822937011719,
        527.400146484375,
        409.8253173828125
      ],
      "text": "Where available, WHO recommends using CXR in parallel with the W4SS, to assist in ruling out TB",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        409.3822937011719,
        527.4400634765625,
        423.8253173828125
      ],
      "text": "disease prior to initiating TPT among people living with HIV who are on ART. The GDG agreed that,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        423.3822937011719,
        527.4376220703125,
        437.8253173828125
      ],
      "text": "due to the increased sensitivity, the evidence supported using CXR in addition to the W4SS as a",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        437.3822937011719,
        527.3661499023438,
        451.8253173828125
      ],
      "text": "parallel screening strategy in which a positive or abnormal result on either screen would indicate a",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        451.3822937011719,
        527.4309692382812,
        465.8253173828125
      ],
      "text": "referral for diagnostic evaluation. Data on “any abnormality” and an “abnormality suggestive of TB”",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        465.3822937011719,
        527.4035034179688,
        479.8253173828125
      ],
      "text": "detected by CXR were reviewed and either approach is recommended, depending on the context,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        479.3822937011719,
        527.4244995117188,
        493.8253173828125
      ],
      "text": "the availability of radiological expertise, resources and preference towards higher sensitivity or higher",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        493.3822937011719,
        116.07279968261719,
        507.8253173828125
      ],
      "text": "specificity.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        521.38232421875,
        527.4058837890625,
        535.8253173828125
      ],
      "text": "The evidence reviewed for the performance of CXR and the W4SS for all people living with HIV came",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        535.38232421875,
        527.421142578125,
        549.8253173828125
      ],
      "text": "from eight studies conducted in Benin, Botswana, Brazil, Guinea, India, Kenya, Malawi, Myanmar,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        549.38232421875,
        527.3892211914062,
        563.8253173828125
      ],
      "text": "Peru, South Africa and Zimbabwe, with a total of 6238 participants. The average prevalence of TB",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        563.38232421875,
        527.3970336914062,
        577.8253173828125
      ],
      "text": "in all people living with HIV in the studies was 7%, ranging from 3% to 18%. Among outpatients on",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        577.38232421875,
        249.09251403808594,
        591.8253173828125
      ],
      "text": "ART, the average prevalence was 2.6%.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        605.38232421875,
        527.4190063476562,
        619.8253173828125
      ],
      "text": "CXR alone was found to have similar sensitivity to and similar or higher specificity than the W4SS",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        619.38232421875,
        527.408935546875,
        633.8253173828125
      ],
      "text": "across all subpopulations. When combined in a sequence whereby CXR followed a positive W4SS",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        633.38232421875,
        527.4147338867188,
        647.8253173828125
      ],
      "text": "screen, CXR had a lower or similar sensitivity with higher or similar specificity. When combined and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        647.38232421875,
        527.3826293945312,
        661.8253173828125
      ],
      "text": "used in parallel with the W4SS, whereby a positive screen from either tool indicates the need for",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        661.38232421875,
        527.42236328125,
        675.8253173828125
      ],
      "text": "a diagnostic test, it had a higher or similar sensitivity and similar specificity (see Table 2.3). The IPD",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        675.38232421875,
        527.4178466796875,
        689.8253173828125
      ],
      "text": "meta-analysis found this strategy to have the highest sensitivity (0.85; 95% CI: 0.69–0.94) compared",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        689.38232421875,
        527.4278564453125,
        703.8253173828125
      ],
      "text": "with the W4SS (0.53; 95% CI: 0.36–0.69) and the other tools and strategies assessed for TB screening",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        703.38232421875,
        527.4476318359375,
        717.8253173828125
      ],
      "text": "in outpatients on ART. While the data were limited for inpatients living with HIV, the combined",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        717.38232421875,
        527.4144287109375,
        731.8253173828125
      ],
      "text": "strategy of CXR and the W4SS had a very low specificity (0.07; 95% CI: 0.03–0.19), similar to findings",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        731.38232421875,
        223.85411071777344,
        745.8253173828125
      ],
      "text": "for using CRP or the W4SS alone.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
